-right-haar-measures","thm-uniqueness-of-left-haar-measure-up-to-scale","cor-normalized-haar-probability-on-a-compact-group","ex-haar-measure-on-an-infinite-product-of-compact-groups"]},{"convention":"Blocks are over the residue splitting field of a splitting p-modular system; a defect group is defined through a diagonal vertex of kGb as a k[G×G]-module.","fixed_by":"def-block-bimodule-for-the-double-group","matters_for":["def-defect-group-and-numerical-defect-of-a-block","thm-defect-zero-blocks-are-simple-algebras","thm-maximal-brauer-pairs-detect-defect-groups"]},{"convention":"Brauer-pair descent is by normal inclusions and relative Brauer maps; the resulting order is independent of the chosen normal chain.","fixed_by":"def-normal-inclusion-of-brauer-pairs","matters_for":["thm-brauer-pair-order-is-independent-of-the-normal-chain","thm-every-brauer-pair-determines-a-unique-global-block","thm-maximal-brauer-pairs-exist-and-are-conjugate"]},{"convention":"GCMs are finite, indexed by I={1,…,n}; rows are coroot-indexed, so α_j(h_i)=a_ij. For symmetrizable A, D has positive diagonal entries and DA is symmetric.","fixed_by":"def-generalized-cartan-matrix","matters_for":["def-realization-of-a-generalized-cartan-matrix","def-simple-reflections-and-the-kac-moody-weyl-group","thm-invariant-bilinear-form-for-a-symmetrizable-kac-moody-algebra","thm-finite-affine-indefinite-trichotomy-for-indecomposable-gcms"]},{"convention":"The Kac–Moody algebra is the quotient of the universal contragredient algebra by its largest Cartan-disjoint ideal; Serre presentation is asserted only for symmetrizable GCMs.","fixed_by":"def-kac-moody-algebra-associated-to-a-gcm","matters_for":["thm-serre-presentation-of-a-kac-moody-algebra","def-kac-moody-verma-module","def-real-and-imaginary-kac-moody-roots","prop-finite-type-kac-moody-algebras-recover-the-dg-semisimple-algebras"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-existence-of-a-left-haar-integral","statement":"Assume AC. Every LCH group admits a nonzero p